28	   - `gold`;
29	   - `status`: `connected`, `disconnected` (with `reservationDeadline`) or `left` (with `exit`, the position its leftover rubbings go to);
30	   - `channel`: a collection or cache claim, with `startTick`, `lastTick` and `heldTicks`;
31	-  - `freshRumors`: the types lost to theft, a flag for the future rumor system.
32	+  - `freshRumors`: the types lost to theft, a flag for the future rumor system;
33	+  - `tonics` (0–2) and `tonicEffect` (the last activation's `startTick` and `endTick`, or null).
34	 - `caches`: id, position and creation tick. A cache never despawns and is removed as soon as it is empty.
35	 - `duels`: the players, `phase` (`fighting`, `choosing` or `settled`), `result`, `choiceDeadline` and `settlement`. A duel is committed once, and settled duels are kept so that a repeated message finds its result.
36	 - `wins`: the last win tick per ordered (winner, loser) pair.
37	-- `goldIssued`: the gold brought in by joining players. Settlements only move gold.
38	+- `goldIssued`: the gold brought in by joining players and minted by grants. Settlements only move gold.
